  "description": "openghg_inversions is the Python package implementing RHIME, the Regional Hierarchical Inversion Modelling Environment, used for regional hierarchical atmospheric Bayesian inversions. The package is developed as part of the OpenGHG project and builds on inversion modelling approaches developed by the Atmospheric Chemistry Research Group at the University of Bristol.",
